{"qas": [
  {"question": "According to arXiv 2405.03855, how do company size and individual executive actions together influence Responsible AI prioritization?", "answer": "Larger companies can offer RAI training, while in smaller or hierarchical companies, a single executive's actions can drive RAI prioritization if they have enough power.", "evidence": [{"page": 7, "quote": "In terms of company size, P9 shares that compared to startups that may try to hire people who already have expertise, their larger company hopes to retain employees for a long time, and can afford to offer training sessions to teach already existing employees about RAI topics."}, {"page": 8, "quote": "The cases where a single individual's desire has been enough is when they have sufficient power (P10), the company is hierarchical (P10), or the company is small enough and leadership is unified in their mission (P7)."}]},
  {"question": "In arXiv 2405.03855, what two strategies are recommended to reduce ethics-washing and improve RAI measurement?", "answer": "Collaboration between RAI experts and journalists for accountability, and developing measurements that include human feedback and connect to concrete harms.", "evidence": [{"page": 9, "quote": "To shift the incentives away from the former to the latter, we suggest greater collaboration between RAI experts and journalists to hold companies accountable and make sense of cheaply made ethics statements."}, {"page": 9, "quote": "Another way to communicate substantive RAI progress is by creating measurements which are more resistant to ethics-washing. These include measurements that incorporate human feedback and connect to more concrete harms (Blodgett et al. 2020; Wang et al. 2022, 2023)."}]},
  {"question": "What is the difference between a Public Benefit Corporation and a Certified B Corporation as defined in arXiv 2405.03855?", "answer": "A Public Benefit Corporation is a legal status, while a Certified B Corporation is a third-party certification by B Lab for social and environmental standards.", "evidence": [{"page": 6, "quote": "Public Benefit Corporations are different from a 'B Corp,' or a Certified B Corporation, which is a third-party certification of social and environmental standards operated by the non-profit B Lab (Koehn 2016)."}]},
  {"question": "According to arXiv 2405.03855, what are the three main obstacles to RAI implementation that affect individual support?", "answer": "Delays to deployment, excessive paperwork, and lack of technical interest are the main obstacles to RAI implementation affecting individual support.", "evidence": [{"page": 9, "quote": "We also find three key components of implementation difficulty that can influence individual support or resistance. Individuals do not like delays to deployment, detest paperwork, and do not find RAI interesting to work on."} ]},
  {"question": "In arXiv 2405.03855, what is one way practitioners make RAI interventions more likely to be adopted, without using the phrase 'path of least resistance'?", "answer": "Practitioners emphasize how easy and quick RAI interventions are compared to traditional processes to encourage adoption.", "evidence": [{"page": 8, "quote": "P15 gives an example from trying to create an internal review system and 'trying to frame it as it's such a quick and easy process. All you have to do is [...]. [It] doesn't take that long and we really pared it down compared to what the traditional university does.'"}]},
  {"question": "How does arXiv 2405.03855 describe the effect of economic downturns on RAI efforts, without using the phrase 'fall through the cracks'?", "answer": "Economic downturns lead to hiring pauses and increased workloads, making it harder for RAI initiatives to progress or even continue.", "evidence": [{"page": 6, "quote": "Relatedly, P[5, 7, 12] specifically discussed recent downward economic forces resulting in company-wide hiring pauses and 'an organizational environment in which people just have more on their plate and it's easier for things to fall through the cracks because there is incentive to focus on different things' (P5). This makes it difficult for RAI efforts to grow or even continue."}]}
]}
